1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:01,212
In 1752,
one wild man

2
00:00:01,212 --> 00:00:02,599
flew a kite
into a storm—

3
00:00:02,599 --> 00:00:04,157
to catch lightning
on a key!

4
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:05,154
Father, stop—

5
00:00:05,154 --> 00:00:06,742
that lightning
bolt could kill us!

6
00:00:06,950 --> 00:00:07,798
Touch the brass key,

7
00:00:07,798 --> 00:00:09,568
William—lightning
is pure electricity!

8
00:00:09,820 --> 00:00:11,469
He bottled real
storm lightning

9
00:00:11,469 --> 00:00:12,623
in a glass
Leyden jar—

10
00:00:12,623 --> 00:00:14,614
naming positive
and negative charge!

11
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:16,411
Then Franklin built

12
00:00:16,411 --> 00:00:17,596
the copper
lightning rod—

13
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:19,146
Whoa! It steered
a thunderbolt

14
00:00:19,146 --> 00:00:20,271
straight
into the earth!

15
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:21,807
One fearless storm test

16
00:00:21,807 --> 00:00:23,133
saved millions
of homes,

17
00:00:23,133 --> 00:00:25,119
and sparked the entire
electric age!

18
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:26,736
Skyscrapers, batteries,

19
00:00:26,736 --> 00:00:27,744
your phone right now—

20
00:00:27,744 --> 00:00:29,504
all trace back
to Benjamin Franklin!
